---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Gallery from '../components/Gallery.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import document from '../../plugin.json';
const command = 'island-cli plugin enable com.sullivansome.spotify';
---
<Site>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="title">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A Spotify plugin for your Mac</p><h1 id="title">Stay in<br />the <span>song.</span></h1><p class="lead">The lyric you’re on. The music you love.<br />A little closer, wherever you’re working.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#setup">Set up the plugin <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#preview">Take a look ↓</a></div><p class="supporting">Requires an Island license + Spotify Desktop · macOS</p></div>
    <div id="preview" class="hero-preview"><Gallery /><p class="preview-note">Your music stays in Spotify.<br />The words come along with you.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="story wrap" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <figure class="expanded-proof"><img src="/previews/expanded.png" width="760" height="360" loading="lazy" alt={document.previews[1].alt} /><figcaption>{document.previews[1].caption}</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="story-copy"><h2 id="story-title">Less switching.<br />More listening.</h2><p>{document.description}</p><dl class="features">{document.features.map(feature => <div><dt>{feature.title}</dt><dd>{feature.description}</dd></div>)}</dl></div>
  </section>
  <section id="setup" class="setup wrap" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Get connected</p><h2 id="setup-title">Your next song<br />starts here.</h2><p>Spotify Lyrics is MIT licensed and ships with Island. Island 1.x costs US$19 once for two Macs, including 1.x updates; future major upgrades are optional. There is no free trial.</p><p>The Island 1.0.0 download supports Apple silicon Macs running macOS 12 or later. <a href="https://island.brighteng.org/pricing/">Pricing and purchase terms ↗</a></p><a class="text-link" href="https://island.brighteng.org/guide/#install">Full Island guide ↗</a></div>
    <div class="setup-content"><ol><li><h3>Enable the plugin.</h3><p>Install Island and activate your key in Settings → License. Then open Market → My plugins → Spotify, or use the bundled CLI.</p><Code label="Enable Spotify in Island" command={command} /></li><li><h3>Open Spotify Desktop.</h3><p>Sign in as usual and play a song. The web player isn’t supported.</p></li><li><h3>Allow Automation.</h3><p>When macOS asks, allow Island to control Spotify. Then return to your music.</p></li></ol><p class="setup-help">Already have Island? Open Market → My plugins to enable Spotify or review a compatible package.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="questions wrap" aria-labelledby="questions-title"><h2 id="questions-title">Before you press play.</h2><div>
    <details><summary>Do I need another Spotify login?</summary><p>No. The plugin reads your local Spotify Desktop session through macOS Automation. It doesn’t ask for your Spotify password.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where do the lyrics come from?</summary><p>LRCLIB and NetEase. Track information is sent to these providers to find synced lyrics. Some songs don’t have a match.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I control playback?</summary><p>Yes: play, pause, previous, and next through the plugin and native companion controls. While the plugin has focus, use Space and the left/right arrow keys.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What access does the plugin have?</summary><p>It runs as a native process with your user privileges. Island’s capability list describes host access; it is not an OS sandbox. macOS separately asks for Spotify Automation permission.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Something isn’t working.</summary><p>Check Automation in System Settings, then restart Island. For incompatible packages, open My plugins and install a current build.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://island.brighteng.org/guide/#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting ↗</a></details>
  </div></section>
</Site>
